# Required: absolute path to your Godot project on the host
GODOT_PROJECT_PATH=/absolute/path/to/your/godot/project

# Directory containing your Claude Code user config (skills/, CLAUDE.md, etc.)
# Defaults to $HOME/.claude if you use the standard Claude Code setup
CLAUDE_USER_CONFIG_DIR=$HOME/.claude

# Godot headless CLI version (default: 4.7.2)
# GODOT_VERSION=4.7.2

# Optional: pin all `docker`/`devcontainer` commands in this project to a
# specific Docker context. Leave unset to use whatever context is currently
# active (the normal default). Only needed if something keeps changing your
# active context out from under you — notably, Docker Desktop resets it to
# "desktop-linux" every time it starts, even if you'd set it to something
# else. If `npm run up` ever behaves like a brand new environment despite no
# real changes, run `docker context ls` to check, then set this to the
# context your container actually lives on.
# DOCKER_CONTEXT=default

# Optional: override MCP/bridge ports. Only needed if running multiple
# instances of this devcontainer in parallel (one clone per Godot project) —
# each clone needs distinct ports. See README "Running multiple instances
# in parallel". Defaults shown; must match the corresponding setting inside
# the Godot project this clone points at (see README).
# GODOT_WS_PORT=6550
# GODOT_LSP_PORT=6005
# GODOT_DAP_PORT=6006
# BLENDER_PORT=9876

# Optional: long-lived Claude Code auth token (from `claude setup-token`).
# Only needed if you ALSO run Claude Code elsewhere on the SAME Anthropic
# account (e.g. on your host). Sharing one account across clients means the
# rotating refresh token gets invalidated by whichever client refreshed last,
# which logs the container out (typically on the first session each day).
# A long-lived token is isolated and avoids that. See README "Staying logged
# in across days". Leave blank/unset to use normal `claude login` (default).
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
